urce":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-109413","namespace":"nvd:cpe","severity":"High","urls":["https://github.com/symfony/symfony/pull/65688","https://github.com/symfony/symfony/security/advisories/GHSA-2v3c-qxhr-7vpv","https://symfony.com/blog/cve-2026-109413-unbounded-recursion-in-the-yaml-inline-lexer-lets-a-single-document-crash-the-process"],"description":"In Symfony YAML prior to versions 5.4.54, 6.4.45, 7.4.18, and 8.1.6, Yaml\\Parser::lexInlineStructure() recursed through lexInlineMapping() and lexInlineSequence() for every { and [ of an inline collection, without entering the nesting level that the rest of the parser bounds with maxNestingLevel. A document made of deeply nested inline collections, such as [[[[...]]]], exhausted the stack while it was being lexed: depending on the PHP version and its stack settings, the process crashed or the request ended with a fatal error.\n\n\n\nAny code parsing untrusted YAML is affected. That includes #[MapRequestPayload] when the Yaml component is installed and the endpoint does not restrict acceptFormat: a single unauthenticated request with a YAML content type is enough.\n\n\n\nThis issue affects symfony/yaml through v5.4.53, v6.0.0-BETA1 through v6.4.44, v7.0.0-BETA1 through v7.4.17, and v8.0.0-BETA1 through v8.1.5.","cvss":[{"source":"596c5446-0ce5-4ba2-aa66-48b3b757a647","type":"Secondary","version":"4.0","vector":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N/E:X/CR:X/IR:X/AR:X/MAV:X/MAC:X/MAT:X/MPR:X/MUI:X/MVC:X/MVI:X/MVA:X/MSC:X/MSI:X/MSA:X/S:X/AU:X/R:X/V:X/RE:X/U:X","metrics":{"baseScore":8.7},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-109413","epss":0.00395,"percentile":0.3394,"date":"2026-11-05"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-109413","cwe":"CWE-674","source":"596c5446-0ce5-4ba2-aa66-48b3b757a647","type":"Secondary"}]}],"matchDetails":[{"type":"exact-direct-match","matcher":"stock-matcher","searchedBy":{"language":"php","namespace":"github:language:php","package":{"name":"symfony